nging to $D$ but *not* $C.$ Note that the elements $-1,0\\in C$ are also in $D,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D∖C & =D-C \\\\  & ={-2,-1,0,1}-{-3,-1,0,5,10} \\\\  & ={-2,1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-1227/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9a9b6de-b0dd-5b38-a32b-378d2b1d86a2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-1227"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105230/selection/2531b01062963bf17cb1953367062769d91dcfc4519f4f6b120c5de4951d40dd" :answer/id #uuid "c8c36e4b-22da-58a0-acd9-04e19f5208f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105230/selection/95645e06230c7ecd851ebb48d1760097d3f7655eeac7335a5df2ed1a72765864" :answer/id #uuid "d047cf23-b809-57ec-a322-b055907c1fb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{4,8,12,16,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105230/selection/5e1635049274c43c908cfb92b91d396d0f79b8adb38ee07d91e5d73b3c468688" :answer/id #uuid "234fb81d-a0c6-5a68-a0cb-b6828e28a816" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2,4,10,14,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105230/selection/b6649e9e1a11c12024c44ab3894aafa3ad4f679e3e89b9df35d0f4500d001796" :answer/id #uuid "7e8c2b53-47eb-52ac-a867-796887360db0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0,2,6,10,14,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105230/selection/01cf34ca11905301f3b3c4b136db1a0aafec5029d8ee6a89ef3d4e87a96402f7" :answer/id #uuid "4de86a42-64e6-58cb-987c-7a350f6c40ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0,4,8,12,16,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105230/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0332e596-2c87-56c9-b761-09e0ed4f7f2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105230/selection/2531b01062963bf17cb1953367062769d91dcfc4519f4f6b120c5de4951d40dd" :answer-field/choices ["q-105230/selection/2531b01062963bf17cb1953367062769d91dcfc4519f4f6b120c5de4951d40dd" "q-105230/selection/95645e06230c7ecd851ebb48d1760097d3f7655eeac7335a5df2ed1a72765864" "q-105230/selection/5e1635049274c43c908cfb92b91d396d0f79b8adb38ee07d91e5d73b3c468688" "q-105230/selection/b6649e9e1a11c12024c44ab3894aafa3ad4f679e3e89b9df35d0f4500d001796" "q-105230/selection/01cf34ca11905301f3b3c4b136db1a0aafec5029d8ee6a89ef3d4e87a96402f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105230" :question/id #uuid "8f8cb276-b659-562e-b6db-d0ae01383b5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-105230" :question/problem "Let $S$  be the set of all multiples of $2$ greater than $0$ and let $T$  be the set of all multiples of $4$ greater than $0.$ What is $T∖S?$" :question/worked-solution "The multiples of $2$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nS={2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nT={4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,36,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $T∖S$ is the *difference* of $T$ and $S,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $T$ but *not* in $S.$\n\nThe elements of $T$ that are also in $S$ are $4,8,12,16,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $4$). So, we must remove these elements from $T.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T∖S & ={4,8,12,16,…}-{2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16,…} \\\\  & =∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-105230/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67e90c94-5018-582f-8692-a1155f41f7c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105230"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86705/selection/2531b01062963bf17cb1953367062769d91dcfc4519f4f6b120c5de4951d40dd" :answer/id #uuid "9da72b15-4218-5bff-8cd6-4b49ad3b4969" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86705/selection/0a5eea1885635b80ee7acd5516d297d115e9ff0b6be4c02e66dcb9a5b8d7b1bd" :answer/id #uuid "606d1dc5-1b35-5479-b925-c7ac318780b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{1,4,16,64,256,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86705/selection/199bf851613ea946edb4e75e8324794a50da9033dd50c48435253896891f6573" :answer/id #uuid "f16879e0-88f6-5e79-bf20-f2b5219274b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86705/selection/22345d8c938f82ac583f286c927f1df7f2c58c3efa1f594611e0eb47917f4930" :answer/id #uuid "82b084e7-de65-5ef1-ae59-2986caad96ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{4,16,64,256,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86705/selection/b6bd6746f786c7573c547754d346d226902b035874b00c58981d5d2d8a3233f1" :answer/id #uuid "a256e1bd-de05-59ae-a0e1-2dc375843e7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{1,2,4,8,16,32,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86705/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "089d9403-e7b6-54bd-a559-438c7b929d25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86705/selection/2531b01062963bf17cb1953367062769d91dcfc4519f4f6b120c5de4951d40dd" :answer-field/choices ["q-86705/selection/2531b01062963bf17cb1953367062769d91dcfc4519f4f6b120c5de4951d40dd" "q-86705/selection/0a5eea1885635b80ee7acd5516d297d115e9ff0b6be4c02e66dcb9a5b8d7b1bd" "q-86705/selection/199bf851613ea946edb4e75e8324794a50da9033dd50c48435253896891f6573" "q-86705/selection/22345d8c938f82ac583f286c927f1df7f2c58c3efa1f594611e0eb47917f4930" "q-86705/selection/b6bd6746f786c7573c547754d346d226902b035874b00c58981d5d2d8a3233f1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86705" :question/id #uuid "0434064c-21b0-5964-ac5a-a3966fbb623a" :question/math-academy-id "q-86705" :question/problem "Let $E$  be the set of all non-negative integer powers of $2$ and let $F$  be  the set of all non-negative integer powers of $4.$  What is $F-E?$" :question/worked-solution "The powers of $2$ that are greater or equal to $1$ are\n\n$$\nE={1,2,4,8,16,32,64,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, the powers of $4$ that are greater or equal to $1$ are\n\n$$\nF={1,4,16,64,256,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $F-E$ is the *difference* of $F$ and $E,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $F$ but *not* in $E.$\n\nAll elements of $F$ are also in $E.$  So, we must remove these elements from $F.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F-E & ={1,4,16,64,256,…}-{1,2,4,8,16,32,64,…} \\\\  & =∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-86705/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67e90c94-5018-582f-8692-a1155f41f7c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86705"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80876/selection/272cdf57d7e1946d1ea86b6c877c57604221ddf0fb86d9bcd6666dcc5d04c5ef" :answer/id #uuid "bbc97d2a-2bb3-50cb-9609-da058b25ee34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{15,30,45,60,75,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80876/selection/157ea35008187f107fd77f4660cac3b05cef5e9f836e87d39f1290b89e5e7eac" :answer/id #uuid "dfd2fced-4366-5e8e-84e6-0b9bbe451fde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{10,20,30,40,50,60,70,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80876/selection/2531b01062963bf17cb1953367062769d91dcfc4519f4f6b120c5de4951d40dd" :answer/id #uuid "ca41bfe1-2185-5f8b-8871-3f8a6ffa3082" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80876/selection/bf5dace0d60a931ff57c6566e0ec4751005697d035fab070164ef58b05927d2e" :answer/id #uuid "5cbf96d1-db2a-5f99-af14-f66f0b10ea22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55,60,65,70,75,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80876/selection/f61cfb65983ebf57b944c3051fd4b0737051393ef293dbcca2b3bb1e5d27c8e9" :answer/id #uuid "fdc7be85-8623-5c7b-a5b1-4833b2027095" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{5,15,25,35,45,55,65,75,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80876/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f57eac1-42c3-57be-8825-0fb0d6c2c319" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80876/selection/2531b01062963bf17cb1953367062769d91dcfc4519f4f6b120c5de4951d40dd" :answer-field/choices ["q-80876/selection/272cdf57d7e1946d1ea86b6c877c57604221ddf0fb86d9bcd6666dcc5d04c5ef" "q-80876/selection/157ea35008187f107fd77f4660cac3b05cef5e9f836e87d39f1290b89e5e7eac" "q-80876/selection/2531b01062963bf17cb1953367062769d91dcfc4519f4f6b120c5de4951d40dd" "q-80876/selection/bf5dace0d60a931ff57c6566e0ec4751005697d035fab070164ef58b05927d2e" "q-80876/selection/f61cfb65983ebf57b944c3051fd4b0737051393ef293dbcca2b3bb1e5d27c8e9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80876" :question/id #uuid "e51fe277-17dd-59c2-bd43-427728072d61" :question/math-academy-id "q-80876" :question/problem "Let $C$  be the set of all multiples of $10$ greater than $0$ and let $D$  be the the set of all multiples of $5$ greater than $0.$ What is $C∖D?$" :question/worked-solution "The multiples of $10$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nC={10,20,30,40,50,60,70,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $5$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nD={5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55,60,65,70,75,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $C∖D$ is the *difference* of $C$ and $D,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $C$ but *not* in $D.$\n\nThe elements of $C$ that are also in $D$ are $10,20,30,40,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $10$). So, we must remove these elements from $C.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C∖D & =C-D \\\\  & ={10,20,30,40,50,60,70,…}-{5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55,60,65,70,75,…} \\\\  & =∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80876/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67e90c94-5018-582f-8692-a1155f41f7c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80876"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-36195"] :question/problem "Let $A$ be the set of all multiples of $10$ greater than $0$ and let $B$ be the set of all multiples of $5$ greater than $0.$ What is $B∖A?$" :question/worked-solution "The multiples of $10$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA={10,20,30,40,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $5$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB={5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $B∖A$ is the *difference* of $B$ and $A,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $B$ but *not* in $A.$\n\nThe elements of $B$ that are also in $A$ are $10,20,30,40,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $10$). So, we must remove these elements from $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B∖A & =B-A \\\\  & ={5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,…}-{10,20,30,40,…} \\\\  & ={5,15,25,35,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7167"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/96cd980d105fe04d2169f9252aa2e7e08bf57ba18cf7d7808d0c4c98c83f7767.png)\n\nGiven the sets $X = \\{ 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 \\}$ and $Y = \\{ 1, 2, 4, 8 \\}$ shown above, find $Y \\setminus X.$" :question/worked-solution "The difference $Y \\setminus X$ consists of all the elements that are in $Y$ but not $X.$ To represent $Y \\setminus X,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $Y$ but not $X.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/5461edca3823f1cafd9f7b51528cd6eb1035e38f7f94c60177e369e2cdd5f350.png)\n\nThe only element in $Y$ that is not in $X$ is $4.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nY \\setminus X = \\{ 4 \\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
